# PlanPathWaypoints.srv
#
# The ROS2-service form of problog_project's PlanWithWaypoints BT node
# (see module/contracts/schema.yaml's own entry) -- the MULTI-WAYPOINT
# generalization of PlanPath.srv's own astar/straight algorithms:
# plans a route from the robot's CURRENT position (read from tf2 by
# the server, same as PlanPath.srv) THROUGH every point in `waypoints`
# IN ORDER, concatenating each leg's own chained-Bezier control points
# into ONE combined chain (planning_core.py's own
# plan_astar_waypoints_points/plan_straight_waypoints_points).
#
# A SEPARATE service from PlanPath.srv, not one more field on it: this
# node's own request shape (a variable-length point LIST instead of one
# goal_x/goal_y pair) is genuinely different, not just one more
# algorithm value sharing the same fields -- see schema.yaml's own
# PlanWithWaypoints entry for the full "why this exists" (shrinking a
# many-leg tree's own compiled ProbLog formula by drawing ONE position-
# noise pair for the whole merged route instead of one per original
# leg) and its own genuine probabilistic-model tradeoff.
#
# Server: amiga_ros2_planners' plan_service_node (same node, same
# obstacle-source state PlanPath.srv's own server already reads --
# see that node's own module docstring).

# One of: "astar", "straight" -- ONLY these two (voronoi has no
# natural per-leg chaining and follow_boarder has no goal point at all
# -- see schema.yaml's own PlanWithWaypoints entry).
string algorithm

# Ordered list of points to visit IN ORDER, world/map frame metres --
# e.g. [(5,27), (41,27), (0,0)] plans (current position) -> (5,27) ->
# (41,27) -> (0,0). At least one point is required; a single-point
# list is equivalent to plain PlanPath's own astar/straight behavior
# (one leg, nothing to chain).
geometry_msgs/Point[] waypoints

---
# Response

# The FULL merged path, chained cubic Bezier control points (length
# 3k+1), in the SAME frame the server read the robot's current pose
# in -- empty if status is false.
geometry_msgs/Point[] control_points

# "completed", "no_path" (waypoints is non-empty but some leg has no
# route), "no_waypoints" (waypoints was empty), or "no_pose" (the
# server couldn't resolve the robot's own current position via tf2).
string reason

# true iff reason is "completed".
bool status
